        "original_id": "0486d9a8-c74e-56c7-97ae-93c0a3f84992",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Makbule Atadan, Mustafa Kemal Atatürk\n- Roles: sister, army officer, revolutionary, founder, President\n- Places: Republic of Turkey\n- Concepts: secularism, nationalism, Kemalism\n\nFacts:\n- Mustafa Kemal Atatürk was born on 19 May 1881.\n- Makbule Atadan was born in 1885.\n- Mustafa Kemal Atatürk was a Turkish army officer, a revolutionary, and the founder of the Republic of Turkey.\n- Makbule Atadan was the sister of Mustafa Kemal Atatürk.\n- Mustafa Kemal Atatürk served as the first President of the Republic of Turkey from 1923 until his death in 1938.\n- Mustafa Kemal Atatürk died on 10 November 1938.\n- Mustafa Kemal Atatürk was ideologically a secularist and a nationalist.\n- The policies and theories of Mustafa Kemal Atatürk became known as Kemalism.\n- Makbule Atadan died on 18 January 1956.",
